    <div id="fallback">
      <h2>The browser is blocking the models</h2>
      <p>Opening the file straight from disk means the browser won't let the page read the <b>.glb</b> files sitting next to it. Either fix works.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink);font-size:13px"><b>A · Serve the folder</b> — best option. In Terminal:</p>
      <code>npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code>
      <p style="margin-bottom:14px">Then open the local URL printed by Astro (normally <b style="color:var(--air)">http://localhost:4321</b>)</p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink);font-size:13px"><b>B · Hand me the files</b> — drop all three here:</p>
      <label class="drop" id="drop">
        <input type="file" id="fin" accept=".glb,model/gltf-binary" multiple hidden>
        <b>Drop the three .glb files</b>
        <span>or click to choose them</span>
      </label>
      <div class="drop-state" id="dstate"></div>
    </div>
